  "details": "   * SECURITY UPDATE: heap corruption on reassembly of an oversized WebSocket\n     message and on sending an oversized WebSocket frame\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-102557-CVE-2026-102559.patch: cap message\n       reassembly and outgoing frames at the GByteArray size limit in\n       process_contents() and send_message() in\n       libsoup/soup-websocket-connection.c, add tests in\n       tests/websocket-test.c\n     - CVE-2026-102557\n     - CVE-2026-102559\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: heap buffer overflow on an oversized incoming WebSocket\n     frame with an unlimited max-incoming-payload-size\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-102558.patch: cap incoming frame payloads at\n       what the receive buffer can hold in process_frame() in\n       libsoup/soup-websocket-connection.c\n     - CVE-2026-102558\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: infinite read loop on WebSocket input, prerequisite of\n     the CVE-2026-102558 fix\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2024-52532.patch: process each frame as soon as\n       data is read in on_web_socket_input() in\n       libsoup/soup-websocket-connection.c\n     - CVE-2024-52532\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: type confusion in the WebSocket pong signal\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-102556.patch: emit the pong signal with a\n       GBytes as declared in receive_pong() in\n       libsoup/soup-websocket-connection.c\n     - CVE-2026-102556",
